    "result_text": "The three files are `AcceptanceBase` (abstract), `AuditLogCapture` (a helper), and `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 so `AcceptanceTest` is the only actual test class, and it passes. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already share today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, following the existing `OwnerCityFullException` pattern:\n\n1. **`OwnerDailyLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending `registrationDate`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100` constant, a `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper, and a check in `addOwner` (after the city-capacity check, before saving) that throws `OwnerDailyLimitException` when the count of existing owners registered on the new owner's `registrationDate` is \u2265 100. The `registrationDate` defaults to `LocalDate.now()` when not supplied, so this enforces the \"created today\" rule.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `OwnerDailyLimitException` returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a ProblemDetail listing `registrationDate` in its `errors`, mirroring the city-full handler.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect the 101st to be 429) passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
